    "description": {
      "source": "https://wwwn.cdc.gov/Nchs/Data/Nhanes/Public/2017/DataFiles/GLU_J.htm",
      "status": "documented",
      "value": "In 2015, diabetes was the seventh leading cause of death in the United States. More than 30 million Americans are living with diabetes, and 86 million are living with prediabetes, which is a serious health condition that increases a person’s risk of type-2 diabetes and other chronic diseases. The prevalence of diabetes and overweight (one of the major risk factors for diabetes) continues to increase. Substantial new efforts to prevent or control diabetes have begun, including the Diabetes Prevention Trial and the National Diabetes Education Program."
    },
